## 2. Editor notes (no number, dose, threshold or clinical claim)

- E1 "Editor note: call the transplant team before changing, holding or stopping any immunosuppressant." Lives in tpe-tma body (once) and critical action 3 (once). Nowhere else on the page.
- E2 "Editor note: open TTP for the microangiopathy work-up, Thrombocytopenia for low platelets and Hemolytic anemia for hemolysis." tpe-tma-links. Links with a reason each.
- E3 "Editor note: related pages are toxicity and levels, brain and PRES and high blood pressure." tpe-tma-links (tpe-cni-toxicity, tpe-pres, tpe-cni-hypertension).
- E4 "Editor note: disposition is decided with the treating transplant team." tpe-tma-links body (last line) and recommendation (last words, outside the bold).

## 3. Gaps awaiting review papers (the page says plainly it does not provide these; they are listed here, not answered)

- How to recognise and differentiate calcineurin inhibitor TMA from TTP, HUS or DIC in a recipient. Labels give a patient-counselling symptom list only (B14).
- Whether and how far to reduce, stop or switch the calcineurin inhibitor. Tacrolimus labels: "consider tacrolimus as a risk factor"; cyclosporine labels: resolution described after reduction or discontinuation, with other treatments.
- Any treatment protocol (plasma exchange, other measures). Cyclosporine labels describe plasmapheresis and streptokinase with heparin only as part of what has occurred, and say management is not clear.
- mTOR inhibitor handling beyond the label sentences.
- Antibody-mediated rejection and complement as causes of TMA. The liver guideline's AMR statement (B19) names thrombocytopenia and hypocomplementemia but not TMA.
- Kidney-recipient specifics (de novo TMA, graft biopsy). Review papers PMC6134269 and PMC10844394 are saved in this folder; not read for this draft by instruction.

## 4. Source differences (stated on the page or overlay; none resolved)

1. Tacrolimus labels name TMA, HUS and TTP and say "consider tacrolimus as a risk factor"; they list risk factors (infections, GVHD, HLA mismatch, calcineurin and mTOR inhibitors) and describe no resolution. Cyclosporine labels describe the syndrome (thrombocytopenia and microangiopathic hemolytic anemia), graft failure, Indium 111 platelet studies and resolution after reduction or discontinuation together with other treatments, and say the pathogenesis and management are not clear; they print no risk-factor list.
2. mTOR: Prograf 5.10 says sirolimus with Prograf "may increase the risk of thrombotic microangiopathy"; Astagraf XL and Envarsus XR print no section on sirolimus (only the 5.14 sentence and counselling 17.9).
3. Section numbers: Prograf 5.16; Astagraf XL and Envarsus XR 5.14. Envarsus XR cross-references the TMA section as 5.13 in section 6 and 17.9 (internal label inconsistency, not used). Envarsus XR names itself ("consider ENVARSUS XR as a risk factor"); Prograf and Astagraf XL say "tacrolimus".
4. Neoral and Gengraf versus Sandimmune: the product name in the resolution sentence ("of cyclosporine" versus "of Sandimmune"); Adverse Reactions, Glomerular Capillary Thrombosis, past tense ("resembled", "included", "post-transplantation") versus present tense ("resemble", "include", "post transplantation").
5. Cyclosporine "Glomerular Capillary Thrombosis" words the pathology as resembling the hemolytic-uremic syndrome; tacrolimus labels name HUS and TTP outright.
6. Heart guideline: one narrative sentence lists TMA with PRES, headache, tremor and seizure as associated with CNI therapy and hypertension; no recommendation. Liver guideline: AMR statement names thrombocytopenia and hypocomplementemia; it does not mention TMA.
7. Hemolytic Anemia consult (App content, row B11) says "Stop the drug" for calcineurin inhibitors in drug-induced TMA; tacrolimus labels say "consider tacrolimus as a risk factor"; cyclosporine labels describe resolution after reduction or discontinuation with other treatments. The page states all three and does not say which is right.

## 5. Statements about existing consults (read from src/data/trees/; not citations)

- hemolytic-anemia.ts line 70 (node hemolytic-anemia-tma body): "Drug-induced TMA: quinine, clopidogrel or ticlopidine, gemcitabine, calcineurin inhibitors. Stop the drug." Shown on the page. Same words in node hemolytic-anemia-danger body, line 41 ("Ask about drugs: ... calcineurin inhibitors (drug-induced TMA) ... Stop the suspect drug."). Same node line 70 also says "High PLASMIC: urgent hematology for plasma exchange"; not shown (no source read here states or cautions on it).
- ttp.ts line 91 (node ttp-plasmic body): table row "Stem cell/solid organ transplant | No transplant history | 1". Shown on the page as a fact; no source read here says how the row applies to a recipient. ttp.ts has no calcineurin, tacrolimus or cyclosporin text (search); lines 133-140 (ttp-ddx-tma) list TTP, HUS, DIC and HELLP without a drug cause.
- thrombocytopenia.ts line 95 (node thrombo-ttp-tma body): "Treat as TTP/TMA until proven otherwise when thrombocytopenia plus MAHA is present." Not shown on the page (no source read here states or cautions on it). Line 187-192 (thrombo-drug) lists drug culprits without calcineurin inhibitors. No transplant text.

## 6. Left out, and why

- Any immunosuppressant dose; any plasma-exchange, complement or antiplatelet advice (no source read here recommends it; the cyclosporine label sentence is quoted as what has occurred).
- Adverse-reaction frequency tables and postmarketing lists naming TMA, HUS or TTP (tacrolimus 6.1 and 6.2): no clinical statement beyond sections 5.14 and 5.16.
- The cyclosporine overdose and nephrotoxicity text: not TMA.
- ISHLT reference list entries on drug-induced TMA (references 474-475): the guideline cites them for the e64 sentence; not read.
- AASLD/AST AMR treatment statements (corticosteroids, immunoglobulin, plasma exchange): about antibody-mediated rejection, not TMA; only the "suspect" sentence is shown, with its grade and scope, so a reader does not take the AMR work-up as a TMA protocol.
- Review papers saved in the folder (TMA_after_renal_transplantation_review_PMC6134269.html, TMA_denovo_kidney_meta_analysis_2024_PMC10844394.html, PRES review PMC4998758): not read, by instruction.
